! MCP, printed p.98 lines 20-37 (MCP_Mar63_001-249 PDF p.105) --
! THE SYN CARDS AT THE TAIL OF THE CONVERSION SUBROUTINE.
!
! Thirty-seven lines on the page.  Lines 1-4 box "CONVERSION
! SUBROUTINE" and lines 5-19 are its fifteen VFL rows; this deck
! takes the TAIL, lines 20-37, which is where every SYN card on the
! page lives.  Four of those lines compile a word and ten are SYN
! cards.  Lines 5-19 are deliberately NOT here: they carry no SYN
! value and they reference LBLZCR and TMX1, which no deck has read,
! so transcribing them would mean back-deriving two symbols from the
! very binary column that is supposed to check the work.
!
! >>> THIS PAGE IS THE AUTHORITATIVE DECLARATION OF SEVEN SYMBOLS
! THAT EXISTING DECKS HAD TO DERIVE, AND IT CONTRADICTS TWO OF
! THEM. <<<
!
!   line 24  STATI  SYN(BU,1),.26   <- pp.69, 70, 78, 79 derived
!                                      0.26 and the (BU,1)
!   line 25  SIMNT  SYN(BU,1),.53   <- pp.70, 75, 79 derived 0.53
!   line 26  S MOUNT SYN(BU,1),.51  <- pp.70, 75, 79 derived 0.51
!   line 27  D FREE SYN,0           <- p.71 wrote "DFREE COMPILES
!                                      ZERO.  It is not defined
!                                      anywhere this project has
!                                      [read]".  HERE IS THE CARD.
!   line 30  SYSMCD SYN(BU,2),SCOMRG+.8   <- p.39 has SYSMCD with
!                                            NO dds.  CONTRADICTION.
!   line 33  S MAXUB SYN,S BA MCP   <- p.40 and p.28 both put
!                                      SMAXUB and SBAMCP at
!                                      (8)2153.0; this card says
!                                      they are the SAME SYMBOL.
!   line 34  SCORG  SYN(BU,1),SCOMRG+.3   <- p.39 has SCORG with
!                                            NO dds.  CONTRADICTION.
!   line 36  X IN END SYN,$         <- pp.13, 15, 17 derived
!                                      (8)5466.0
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE DATA DESCRIPTION COLUMN IS PRINTED IN OCTAL
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The column between BINARY OUTPUT and NAME prints mode, LENGTH and
! BYTE SIZE.  Line 24's card says SYN(BU,1) and the column says
! "BU,01 ,10"; line 30's says SYN(BU,2) and the column says
! "BU,02 ,10".  A byte size of 0o10 is 8 bits, which is the STRAP
! default, so the column is OCTAL.  Printed p.84 line 7 is the same
! reading from the other end -- SYN(BU,48) printing "BU,60 ,10",
! and 0o60 is 48.
!
! FIVE OF THE TEN CARDS ARE DOUBLE-ATTESTED that way, because the
! dds appears in the STATEMENT column too: lines 24, 25, 26, 30 and
! 34.  TWO REST ON THE OCTAL READING ALONE and are flagged as such:
!
!   line 20  L XA    "BU,1CC,1C"  ->  (BU,64,8)
!   line 33  S MAXUB "B ,31 ,01"  ->  (B,25,1), inherited from
!                                     S BA MCP, which this page does
!                                     not declare
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! SUBSTITUTIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  The NAME column prints "S MOUNT", "D FREE", "Z FINIS",
!     "S MAXUB", "X IN END", "L XA", "Y BCRD"; the STATEMENT column
!     on line 33 prints "S BA MCP" for SBAMCP.
!
! (2) "SCCRG" IS WRITTEN SCORG, AND THE GLYPH IS DISPUTED.  Line
!     34's NAME column prints five characters with no blank, and at
!     1800 dpi characters 2 and 3 are IDENTICAL open-right C's --
!     the ink says SCCRG.  It is read as SCORG on an argument that
!     does not depend on any glyph: line 34's LOCATION is 002151.03,
!     and printed p.39 line 19 ("CM0000(BU,1),SCORG") has a left
!     address of 002151.03.  Same bit, same symbol.  Corroborating
!     but weaker: p.39 line 19's own STATEMENT renders at 1800 dpi
!     with a CLOSED O, plainly different from the open C beside it,
!     on the same row off the same printer; and line 34's own
!     statement column prints "SCOMRG+.3" with a closed O two
!     characters along.  Recorded as a DISPUTED GLYPH, resolved
!     symbol.
!
! (3) A SYN VALUE WRITTEN ".26" IS WRITTEN 0.26.  The listing writes
!     the word number as empty where it is zero; p.62's deck already
!     writes those as "0.00".
!
! (4) NOTHING ELSE.  Every other glyph reads cleanly at 600 dpi.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ONE LISTING MARK: line 29 carries the bare "*" after its location
! ("005465.00 *") that printed pp.3, 37, 38 and 39 also carry.  It
! changes no compiled bit.  (Line 6, outside this block, carries a
! second.)
!
! ROWS DELIBERATELY ABSENT, as printed p.24 established: a SYN row
! prints its VALUE in the location column and no word, so the ten
! SYN cards are checked in SYMBOLS rather than in the row list.

! ---- from pages already transcribed -------------------------------
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)2151.0               ! printed p.37 line 11, "THE
                                      !   SYSTEM WORD FLAG"
SBAMCP  SYN, (8)2153.0               ! printed p.28; line 33 below
                                      !   says SMAXUB IS this symbol
! ---- read off line 20's OWN location and dds columns ---------------
! The listing prints TMLXA nowhere on this page; line 20's location
! is 000034.00+ and its dds "BU,1CC,1C".  THE VALUE IS FROM THE INK;
! THE READING IS NOT: 0o34 is word 28, and word 28 is index register
! $12 only by the Stretch index-register layout, which this page does
! not state.  Nothing checked here depends on it -- TMLXA and LXA
! resolve to the same bit either way.  Printed p.83 line 22 appears to
! carry the declaration itself and is the page to check when p.83 is
! read.
TMLXA   SYN, (8)34.0

        SLC, (8)5464.0

LXA     SYN, TMLXA                   ! line 20
        CNOP                         ! line 21 -- pads nothing.  Line
                                      !   19's printed location is
                                      !   005463.40 and it is a
                                      !   half-word B, so the counter
                                      !   reaches this card already at
                                      !   005464.00.  That location was
                                      !   rendered but line 19 itself is
                                      !   not transcribed here.

! ---- ADDITIONS MADE TO MAKE ASSIGNMT. COMPATIBLE (line 22) --------
YBCRD   BD, $                        ! line 23 -UNCODE PATH NOT TO
                                      !           BE TAKEN
STATI   SYN(BU,1), 0.26              ! line 24
SIMNT   SYN(BU,1), 0.53              ! line 25
SMOUNT  SYN(BU,1), 0.51              ! line 26
DFREE   SYN, 0                       ! line 27
YLCL2   VF                           ! line 28
YLCL1   VF                           ! line 29
SYSMCD  SYN(BU,2), SCOMRG+.8         ! line 30 -TWO BIT OPERATIONG
                                      !           MODE
STERMI  VF, ZFINIS                   ! line 31 -THE LAST LOC USED
                                      !           BY MCP
ZFINIS  SYN, (8)17777.0              ! line 32
SMAXUB  SYN, SBAMCP                  ! line 33 -MAX UB+1 THAT CAN
                                      !           BE USED
SCORG   SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.3         ! line 34 -TH+ COMPILE GO BITS
        CNOP                         ! line 35
XINEND  SYN, $                       ! line 36
        UNTAIL, (2)                  ! line 37
        END, YBCRD

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKED ROWS -- the four that compile a word.  The ten SYN
! cards print a VALUE and no word, and are checked in SYMBOLS below,
! which is the stronger place for them (printed p.24's convention).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line 23  005464.00  005464.04 00                 Y BCRD BD,$
!   line 28  005464.40  000000.00+                   Y LCL2 VF
!   line 29  005465.00  000000.00+                   Y LCL1 VF   (*)
!   line 31  005465.40  017777.00+                   S TERMI VF,ZFINIS
!
! THE CHECKED SYMBOLS -- the location column of every SYN card, and
! the four labels.  The listing prints these in OCTAL word.bit.
!   L XA     000034.00     line 20
!   Y BCRD   005464.00     line 23
!   STATI    000000.32     line 24   0o32 = bit 26
!   SIMNT    000000.65     line 25   0o65 = bit 53
!   S MOUNT  000000.63     line 26   0o63 = bit 51
!   D FREE   000000.00     line 27
!   Y LCL2   005464.40     line 28
!   Y LCL1   005465.00     line 29
!   SYSMCD   002151.10     line 30   0o10 = bit 8 past SCOMRG
!   S TERMI  005465.40     line 31
!   Z FINIS  017777.00     line 32
!   S MAXUB  002153.00     line 33
!   SCORG    002151.03     line 34   bit 3 past SCOMRG
!   X IN END 005466.00     line 36
